    "text": "Good morning, listeners tuning in across the United States — you’re with Alex and Jordan on Audexa Radio, and it’s time for a gaming deep dive. Today we’re looking beyond the usual blockbuster trailer cycle, because some of the most interesting gaming stories are about the tools, communities, and strange experiments shaping what games can become. Jordan, where do we start?",
    "type": "intro"
  },
  {
    "speaker": "host2",
    "text": "Let’s start with Newgrounds, which is one of those platforms that can feel like a time capsule and a living laboratory at the same time. The community site, known for games, music, animation, and art, drew major attention on Hacker News. That matters because Newgrounds represents a version of the internet where creators could publish directly, find an audience, and build a following without first passing through a major platform’s approval process.",
